This test was inspired by an example described in Section 2.1 of:

https://jeanlachaud.com/research/NASA_CR-2015-218960.pdf

The test there is actually really poorly described, but I figured I'd give it a
try anyway.  The problems consists of a 5 cm bar of unspecified TPS material
that has a temperature BC applied to one end.  The bar starts at 300 K, and the
right end of the bar is put in contact with 1644 K for 60 seconds, and the 300K
for 60 seconds.  Temperature is extracted over that time at several points in
the right half of the bar.  No material properties were specified, so I just
found nominal thermal properties for TPS materials.

To make this work, I had to make a small modification to RigidMPM.cc.  The
patch file is in this directory, RigidMPM.cc.patch.  This just makes a dynamic
change to the boundary temperature at 60 seconds.  The boundary temperature
is imposed using an additional material and the <thermal_contact> 
option.

A simple script to extract the temperature over time at several points is
included here as well, extractTemp.csh.  The results can then be plotted
using the gnuplot inplot file included here as well.  Results are shown in
the included .png file.
